meta.description:
Connects the Jingshu mobile app to DSH on this computer: installs the host-side bridge once (relay, credentials, reverse calls, outbox) and exposes a local pairing-status endpoint.

Where the login code is: it is not shown here. The bridge writes it to %USERPROFILE%\.dsbot\pair.json and rotates it every 10 minutes. Any of these works:
1) run tools\jingshu-pair.ps1 (add -Open to open the QR page);
2) open %USERPROFILE%\.dsbot\pair.html in a browser (auto-refreshes every 30 seconds, shows the QR code);
3) request http://127.0.0.1:<DSH port>/jingshu-host/pair with a DSH session.

If the phone keeps disconnecting, the bridge is down: run schtasks /run /tn DSBotBridge or tools\jingshu-pair.ps1 -Restart, then read a fresh code.
